From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:25:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/42] cuda: GDN -- a multi-sequence ubatch with snapshots (K
 > 1, MTP) takes the chunked prefix + sequential tail per sequence
 (GGML_CUDA_GDN_MULTISEQ_TAIL=0: off)

The chunked ops keep the full per-sequence row stride (seq_tokens) of g/beta/attn_out when they process a
prefix, and the sequential kernel takes the attn rows' per-sequence stride (attn_seq_tokens), so the
n_seqs == 1 prefix + tail split now also serves n_seqs > 1 with K > 1.  Before, such a ubatch ran the whole
sequential kernel (~1.45 ms per call on a 2 x 34K concurrent prefill vs ~0.14 ms chunked).  Every existing
call is unchanged (n_seqs == 1: sequence 0; K == 1 multi-seq: no limit, seq_tokens == n_tokens).

Prod config (Flash-Next UD-IQ4_XS, MTP, -sm tensor, -ub/-b 4096), on / off: two fresh prompts at once
39K + 34K 22.8 -> 22.0 s, 59K + 59K 37.4 -> 36.1 s, 2 x 34K 20.3 -> 19.8 s; greedy 1237e15cbaf5 and pdecs
5c5fdcc9338a unchanged.  FINDINGS 1167/1169.
